COURSE.find(c=>c.id==='crashcourse').stages[1].html += `<details class="scaffold"><summary>Rhetorical toolkit · precise terms, specific effects</summary><dl><dt>Anaphora</dt><dd>Repeating a beginning across successive clauses. In §5, the repeated “Nobody” turns apparently harmless individual responses into a collective pattern of neglect.</dd><dt>Metaphor</dt><dd>Describing one thing as another. The “family” in §4 implies care and mutual obligation; the neglected entrance tests that promise.</dd><dt>Antithesis / contrast</dt><dd>Setting opposing ideas against each other. Visibility and invisibility in §6 connect public recognition with the erasure of work.</dd><dt>Parallelism</dt><dd>Using repeated grammatical structures. The two “If” clauses in §6 balance different costs of the decision.</dd><dt>Irony</dt><dd>A gap between a stated ideal and the situation presented. The inclusive banner contrasts with the overlooked side entrance.</dd><dt>First-person narration</dt><dd>A narrative choice, not a rhetorical figure. Access to Leila’s doubts encourages closeness while limiting what can be known about other people’s intentions.</dd></dl></details>`;
